vey in an older bi-racial community population</article-title><source>Ann Epidemiol</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9669617</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rimer</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Conaway</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyna</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rakowski</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Woods-Powell</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Tessaro</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>12</volume><issue>5</issue><year>1996</year><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>357</lpage><article-title>Cancer screening practices among women in a community health center population</article-title><source>Am J Prev Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8909646</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Paskett</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>DeGraffinreid</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tatum</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Margitic</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><volume>25</volume><issue>5</issue><year>1996</year><fpage>547</fpage><lpage>553</lpage><article-title>The recruitment of African-Americans to cancer prevention and control studies</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8888322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="book"><source>SPA employees by race/ethnicity [Internet]</source><publisher-loc>Raleigh</publisher-loc><publisher-name>North Carolina Office of State Personnel</publisher-name><access-date>cited 2006 Jul 31</access-date><comment>Available from:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http:/